  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Floods Response Coordination &amp; Recovery in Rufiji and Kibiti Districts, Coast Region,   Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The six-month Initiation Plan by the UNDP Country Office in Tanzania targets enhancing disaster preparedness and response capabilities across severely flood-affected regions, particularly Rufiji and Kibiti districts. The plan focuses on improving coordination among government agencies, local communities, and international partners for a unified disaster response. It also involves conducting detailed needs assessments tailored to the specific challenges of these areas, alongside capacity-building</narrative>
  </description>
